sentences.l:
And she, when now she reached the suitors, heavenly-one of women,
stood then beside the doorpost of the close-built roof,
before her cheeks holding her shining veil;

But going into the house, tend to your own tasks,
the loom and the distaff, and to the handmaids give orders
to ply their work;

and at dawn let us go and sit down in assembly,
all of us, so that to you I may declare a speech without softening,
to go forth from the halls;

But if to you it seems this thing more profitable and better
to be, one man’s livelihood unavenged to destroy,
then despoil it;

But indeed there are kings of the Achaeans, other ones too,
many, in sea-girt Ithaca, young and old,
of whom one may have this, since heavenly Odysseus has died;
